  "needs_manual_review": true,
  "needs_manual_review_reason": "Series-level GEO metadata verified directly against the live source; per-sample clinical/pathology fields (grade, sex/age, anatomic location, brain invasion, treatment timepoint) have not yet been extracted from individual GSM records or supplementary tables -- part of the batch-1 scaling pass, prioritizing breadth of verified accessions over per-sample depth. Publication metadata pulled from PubMed esummary; not yet manually spot-checked against the full text for every record in this batch. FACT-CHECK UPDATE (2026-07-12 re-verification pass): raw_data_available corrected from 'Not reported' to true; the live series provides raw sequencing data via SRA (SRP348182 / BioProject PRJNA784116) plus GSE189672_RNAseq_raw_counts.csv.gz. Confirmed all 110 GSMs carry only tissue='meningioma tumor' at the GSM level (grade/sex/age live only in the GSE189672_Clinical_data.xlsx supplement), so those demographic fields remain 'Not reported' at the GEO metadata level. Publication (PMID 35108039, Science advances 2022, DOI 10.1126/sciadv.abm6247) re-verified via PubMed this pass. DEEP AUDIT 2026-07-14: the prior passes correctly noted that GSM-level characteristics only carry tissue='meningioma tumor' and left grade/sex/age/location/brain-invasion/molecular-subtype/outcome fields as 'Not reported', but never actually opened the series' own GSE189672_Clinical_data.xlsx supplementary file to check whether those fields existed there instead (they had only checked GSM characteristics, not the supplement). Downloaded and directly parsed that file (xlsx, 110 data rows, columns: Sample/MenG/Gender/Age/MIB/WHO grade/Brain Invasion/Necrosis/Location/Simpson_grade/ResectionType/Recurrence/MonthsFollowUp/WES/RNA-seq/Methylation/PLS/Ch1pLoss/Ch22Loss/TotalChrDeletions/NF2_LogExp/NF2/SMARCB1/TRAF7/KLF4/AKT1/PIK3CA/SMO/POLR2A/ARID1A/TERT Promoter Mutation). This is a substantial, previously-missed per-sample clinical/genomic dataset covering all 110 samples: (1) grade_breakdown corrected from all-null to 90 WHO I / 20 WHO II / 0 WHO III (sums to 110), tags.grade_comparable corrected false->true. (2) molecular_subtype_annotated corrected from 'Not reported' to true: the 'MenG' column assigns every sample to one of three named molecular groups (MenG A=52, MenG B=26, MenG C=22, Unknown=10), exactly the paper's own 'three biologic groups of meningioma (MenG A, B, and C)' that the live GEO series_summary itself describes as identifiable through DNA methylation/RNA-seq/cytogenetic profiling; the sheet additionally carries per-sample driver-gene mutation calls (NF2/SMARCB1/TRAF7/KLF4/AKT1/PIK3CA/SMO/POLR2A/ARID1A/TERT), reinforcing this is a genuine molecular classification, not a histological-grade proxy. tags.molecular_subtype_annotated corrected false->true. (3) has_outcome_data corrected from 'Not reported' to true: the sheet carries a per-sample 'Recurrence' column (91 N / 19 Y) and a 'MonthsFollowUp' column (continuous follow-up duration, present for all 110 rows), i.e. genuine deposited recurrence-free-survival/follow-up data, not merely an abstract-level prognostic claim (the failure pattern this project has caught twice before on other records, e.g. the Hertie-Institute case in docs/methodology.md); tags.has_outcome_data corrected false->true. tags.recurrence_annotated is deliberately left false: this 'Recurrence' column is a clinical follow-up outcome for patients whose tumor was resected as a PRIMARY specimen (the series' own overall_design states all 110 are 'primary meningiomas'), not a primary-vs-recurrent-SAMPLE split (no recurrent-tumor specimens were profiled), so it is has_outcome_data territory, not recurrence_annotated, per the schema's distinction. (4) brain_invasion.status_reported corrected false->true: the 'Brain Invasion' column is populated for all 110 rows (uniformly 'N', i.e. 0 of 110 recorded as brain-invasion-positive); counts field updated accordingly. determination_method left 'Not reported': the linked paper's methods (fetched via Europe PMC full text, PMC11313601) state only that 'presence of brain invasion' was one of several variables reviewed under an IRB-approved chart-review protocol, without specifying histological vs. radiographic assessment, so tags.brain_invasion_annotated is deliberately left false (status_reported alone is not sufficient per the schema, a stated determination method is also required, and none is stated). (5) treatment_timepoint_status corrected from ['Not reported'] to ['primary'], consistent with the series' own explicit 'primary meningiomas' framing and the clinical table containing no recurrent-sample rows. (6) sex_distribution (67 F / 43 M), age_distribution (n=110, range 19-81, mean 57.8), anatomic_location_breakdown (per-site counts across 16 named sites), and patient_count (110, one row per patient/sample, no multi-sample patients evident in the sheet) all filled in from the same file, previously 'Not reported'. All figures independently tabulated from the raw xlsx (parsed via its underlying XML, not trusted from any summary), not from the paper's prose. SAMPLE-LEVEL TABLE ADDED (2026-07-14): re-downloaded the same GSE189672_Clinical_data.xlsx fresh and parsed all 110 rows into the new optional `samples` field (one row per sample: sample_id, sex, age, who_grade, anatomic_location, outcome [Recurrence + MonthsFollowUp], molecular_subtype [MenG group]) -- this is the pilot for a new per-sample browsing table feature on the website, modeled on the ScPCA Portal's sample-level pages. This is genuine per-sample source data, not derived/estimated from the aggregate counts already in this record. ONTOLOGY ADDED (2026-07-14): disease_id=MONDO:0016642, tissue_ids=['UBERON:0003547'], both verified live against the EBI Ontology Lookup Service (ols4/api/search) before use, not guessed. Generic term: this 110-sample cohort spans all three WHO grades and many named anatomic sites (see the new samples field), with no single distinguishing subtype/site to warrant a more specific MONDO term.",
